+   /**
+    * First spot above the pad with room to stand.
+    *
+    * The old code always landed you at pad + 3. That was survivable only because the move was
+    * done with setPosition, which never told the client: the server saw the whole jump as one
+    * delta, kicked you for moving too quickly, and the reconnect quietly resynced you onto solid
+    * ground. Now that the move is a real teleport, pad + 3 is where you actually end up -- and
+    * under any ceiling, that is inside the rock.
+    *
+    * Scan up from the pad instead and take the first gap tall enough to stand in.
+    */
+   /**
+    * Where to stand when arriving on top of a teleporter, or -1 if the space is not clear.
+    *
+    * Just the column directly above the block -- no searching. The old version scanned eight
+    * blocks upward for any gap it could find, so a teleporter with anything above it put the
+    * arriving player through the ceiling and onto the roof of their own base, and when it found
+    * nothing it fell back to y+3, which can be inside a wall. Anything cleverer than "is the
+    * space above clear" ends up moving people somewhere they did not ask to go.
+    *
+    * Only the two blocks a player actually occupies have to be free, so an ordinary two-high
+    * room still works.
+    */
+   private static double standingRoomAbove(World world, int x, int y, int z) {
+      if (world.getBlockId(x, y + 1, z) != 0 || world.getBlockId(x, y + 2, z) != 0) {
+         return -1.0;
+      }
+
+      return y + 1;
+   }
